  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Unsettled weather and cooler temperatures today \nthrough the weekend.\n\nUpper level trough and associated closed low currently over the \nnorthern Great Lakes early this morning will dive further southeast \nacross the central Great Lakes today before lifting northeast across \nNew England Saturday night. As such surface low pressure centered \nover central Ontario will continue to progress east, bringing its \nattendant cold front across the area today. Ahead of the front, \nexpect another cloudy day with scattered showers to pass across the \narea. In the wake of the cold frontal passage and on the back side \nof the surface low tonight through Saturday, cool moist air will \nwrap around to further support lake enhanced showers downwind of the \nlakes Saturday.\n\nThe next upper level trough will dive southeast across the upper and \ncentral Great Lakes Sunday supporting a surface low to cross east \nacross northern Ontario and Quebec, where a pair of fronts approach \nthe region Sunday and Sunday night. Ahead of the fronts, lake \nenhanced showers will persist east of both lakes during the day on \nSunday before more widespread precipitation arrives Sunday night.",
